    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW27ctbJ968Ep7DYfsGqXU6xM)_\n\nBuilds on #332 (`sp-litnotes-meta-backfill-children`) and the `book-sections` / `collection-articles` views from #330.\n\n## What changes\n- `C-u M-x sp-litnotes-meta-backfill-children`, or the new `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-backfill-all-children`, makes the notes of every BibTeX entry that cross-references the book. Nothing is picked. If nothing is missing, the table is still created or refreshed.\n- Afterwards, in the book/collection note: the new notes are added to the Vulpea database, a `collection-query-table` block is inserted above the first heading if the note has none (`book-sections`, or `collection-articles` for `collection`/`mvcollection`/`proceedings`/`mvproceedings`), and the block is updated. An existing block is only updated. The note is saved if it had no unsaved changes.\n- Literate doc updated (bullets); two new ERT tests.\n\n## Testing\n- `sp-litnotes-meta` ERT tests pass (12/12, Emacs 29.3, stubbed citar/Vulpea). `tools/check-tangle.sh` passes.\n- Not run on the real vault or with the real Vulpea DB.\n\n## Follow-up option\nBibTeX children that have no note yet are not rows in the table; only existing notes appear. If you also want those shown as placeholder rows, that is a separate change.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAsbQDho5VHotsU68a)_",
